<includes>

    <!-- ── TinyPPI overlay font selector (by ABUKARIM TOOLS) ──
         font23_narrow / font32 are the two font NAMES the TinyPPI overlay
         (script-tinyppi-main.xml) references. The actual .ttf is USER-SELECTABLE
         via ActivateWindow(1118) (font picker -> DialogCustom_Settings_Items_TinyPPIFont),
         which writes Skin.String(tinyppi.font) then ReloadSkin()s.

         Kodi's font <filename> must be a literal string (no $INFO/$VAR expansion
         at font-load time), AND a "condition" attribute is only honoured on an
         <include> that REFERENCES A NAMED include - not on a raw <font> and not
         on an anonymous inline <definition>. So each candidate is its own NAMED
         include (two <font> blocks, both names -> the one chosen .ttf), and
         Font_Static pulls in exactly one via a conditional reference. The
         __Default one restores the original Noto-Regular/Noto-Bold split and is
         emitted whenever the string is empty or not one of the 8. Sizes stay
         22/30 to match the original overlay. -->

    <!-- Each candidate sets ALL overlay font names to the one chosen .ttf:
           * font_tiny_iconic_regular1  -> the AF3 legacy PPI value labels (the
             big Latin text in the ActivateWindow(1118)/DialogPlayerProcessInfo
             overlay). THIS is what the screenshot shows.
           * font10_bold                -> legacy PPI section headers (was
             undefined -> Kodi fell back to the oversized font13).
           * font23_narrow / font32     -> the separate TinyPPI *script* overlay.
         Value labels at size 20 (down from the stock iphone.ttf@24, which
         renders oversized); headers 22 bold. -->
    <include name="TinyPPI_Font_AmazonEmber">
        <font><name>font_tiny_iconic_regular1</name><filename>AmazonEmberV2-Bold.ttf</filename><size>20</size></font>
        <font><name>font10_bold</name><filename>AmazonEmberV2-Bold.ttf</filename><size>22</size></font>
        <font><name>font23_narrow</name><filename>AmazonEmberV2-Bold.ttf</filename><size>22</size></font>
